Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-02-2000||02:57 AM||||HELP! My latest Fiero that Im restoring (88 Formula) will start fine, and run like a champ, for about 5 minutes...then it just dies and wont recrank until like 1 1/2 or so. Ive heard (from a very reliable source) that its prob. my ignition module...what do you think? please help! Thanx||||reg||5
Z||000001||DiggityDan||06-02-2000||03:38 PM||||I have a tendency to think its fuel related, probably fuel pump or maybe even a bad fuel pressure regulator. After it dies, are you turning the key off and on trying to get it restarted? If you are, you are pumping up the fuel system and then it starts and runs out of pressure. Try hooking up a pressure gauge before you start it so you can see what your fuel pressure is actually doing. Or if you don't have one, push the schrader valve that's on top of the engine - justput a rag over it first so incase I'm wrong gas doesn't get in your eyes. <BR>Let us know if you find something out||||reg||1
